 know is that  they have expected this for a long time  and that they have tried to prepare as  well as possible for uh for for quite a  few weeks now and all this discussion  about heavy Weaponry that we've been  hearing the delivery of new weapons all  this was meant to fight back an assault  on donbass from the Russian side right  and what if Mario Paul we've been  following events there for weeks and  Pentagon says it has seen a  concentration of airstrikes and  artillery there  yeah we know that the last part of the  Ukrainian Army that are still in the  city are in this steel works this  gigantic steel works that was a symbol  of the city and they are staying there  there's a huge bunker underneath a  system of tunnels and civilians are also  hiding there what we've been hearing but  it's unconfirmed is that many of these  civilians are the relatives of these  soldiers because they are afraid that  they might be a target for the Russian  army as well  it seems that the Army is still there in  this very small part of town and it's  heavily bombed we've seen pictures  but for the moment it's as it has been a  war of attrition a very cruel War of  Attrition in mariupo right and and How  likely is it that Ukrainian forces will  be able to defend uh Mario Paul and keep  the Russians out  well the only way to do that would be  another offensive uh from coming from  another side and and this opening uh a  courage uh breaking the blockade of the  city  um we haven't seen any offensive in that  uh direction we haven't seen any  preparations for that so um it seems  that the Ukrainian Army is not able to  do that at the moment  and civilians of course caught up in all  of this how are they dealing with this  increase in hostilities  the Ukrainian authorities have called  upon civilians to leave these areas in  donbass that are likely to be uh the  theater of the next uh escalation  um we have also seen that there were  trains to bring out people we don't know  how many 